    'Prepare a handoff that survives a change of shift: last known healthy state, current user impact, actions completed, action in progress, open risks, links to approved records, and the next decision time. Redact tokens, personal information, and customer content from messages and screenshots. If an external dependency or disclosure question is involved, escalate to the named owner instead of improvising. After recovery, review the messages for delayed ownership, ambiguous status, or unsupported certainty. Update the template and runbook with the smallest improvement. The offshore developer can strengthen evidence capture and continuity; incident command and communications authority stay with the approved internal roles.',
